//ERR 11 3 11 20
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// The check runs over instances, after types are known, so a template is
// checked once per instantiation. The body here is missing a return whatever
// `T` turns out to be, and the i32 instance is rejected.
//
// The span covers the declaration's signature, `pick[T] x: T flag`, not the
// `pick[i32](5 false)` that caused the instance to exist — the fix belongs in
// the body, so that is where the error points.

fn pick[T] x: T flag
    if flag
        ret x

fn main
    out "{pick[i32](5 false)}"
